  "question": {
    "text": "Let three vectors $\\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{a}}=\\alpha \\hat{i}+4 \\hat{j}+2 \\hat{k}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{b}}=5 \\hat{i}+3 \\hat{j}+4 \\hat{k}, \\overrightarrow{\\mathrm{c}}=x \\hat{i}+y \\hat{j}+z \\hat{k}$ form a triangle such that $\\vec{c}=\\vec{a}-\\vec{b}$ and the area of the triangle is $5 \\sqrt{6}$. If $\\alpha$ is a positive real number, then $|\\vec{c}|^2$ is equal to:",
    "image": null
  },
